------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The GPU hardware video paths (NVIDIA NVENC/NVDEC, AMD AMF, Intel QSV/oneVPL)
are implemented as **hand-rolled FFI in this repository** (under
crates/codec/src/{encode,decode}/), declared against the respective vendor SDK
headers (NVIDIA Video Codec SDK, AMD AMF SDK, Intel oneVPL) and loading the
vendor runtime libraries dynamically at runtime via dlopen. The underlying
vendor SDKs are proprietary and are not redistributed with this software. No
third-party GPU wrapper crates are used.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MP3 encoding, when built with the `lame` feature (off by default), uses LAME
(https://lame.sourceforge.io/, LGPL-2.0-or-later), which is NOT linked into or
distributed with this software: it is loaded from the host at run time via
dlopen (libmp3lame.so.0 / libmp3lame.dylib / libmp3lame.dll, or the path in
RIVET_LAME_LIBRARY), in the same way as the GPU vendor runtimes above. A
build without the feature contains no code that loads it. Whoever installs
and distributes the LAME library is responsible for its LGPL obligations.

The AAC-LC encoder and decoder (crates/aac, the rivet-aac repository,
https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-aac, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author, written from
the ISO/IEC 13818-7 and 14496-3 standards and published literature (see
docs/decisions.md, section 26, and that repository's docs/PROVENANCE.md).
They do not include or derive from any third-party AAC encoder or decoder.
Their normative tables were transcribed from a copy of ISO/IEC 13818-7:2004,
as docs/decisions.md section 26 records. They do not implement spectral band
replication, parametric stereo or USAC (HE-AAC, HE-AAC v2, xHE-AAC); an
HE-AAC stream decodes as its AAC-LC core. AAC may be subject to patent
licensing in some jurisdictions; Via LA administers a licensing programme
for AAC. This software grants no patent rights and makes no claim about
whether a licence is needed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The FLAC and ALAC (Apple Lossless) audio decoders and encoders (under
crates/codec/src/audio/{lossless,decode,encode}/) are original implementations
written for this project from the FLAC format specification (IETF RFC 9639),
the published Apple Lossless format description, and published literature on
linear prediction and Rice coding. They contain no code from libFLAC, FFmpeg,
Apple's ALAC reference implementation or any other codec implementation. The
Apple Lossless format was published by Apple Inc. under the Apache License,
Version 2.0; FLAC is an open, royalty-free format.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This software also uses a number of additional open-source Rust crates from
the broader ecosystem, distributed under permissive licenses (predominantly
MIT and/or Apache-2.0; some BSD/ISC). A full machine-readable inventory of
the dependency tree and its licenses can be produced with `cargo metadata`
or `cargo about`. Notable ones include: tokio, anyhow, thiserror, tracing,
bytes, clap, mp4, matroska-demuxer, libloading, tempfile (MIT/Apache-2.0);
minimp3 (MIT), lewton (MIT/Apache-2.0), audiopus (ISC, binding to libopus
under the BSD license), rubato (MIT), md5 (MIT/Apache-2.0); and, when the `ffmpeg` feature is
enabled, ffmpeg-next (binding to FFmpeg, which is LGPL-2.1+/GPL-2+ — review
its obligations before distributing an `ffmpeg`-enabled build).
